-- `invalid_entry_file` (boundary.md §5.2): a platform may declare the entry
-- file's name, and a declared name must be one no module can take — one path
-- segment beginning with `_` and ending in `.mjs`. This platform declares
-- `main.mjs`, which is exactly the name the module `Main` already folds onto
-- (backend.md §2, rule 1), so moving the name into the manifest would have
-- let a platform author put the old defect back in data. It is refused when
-- the platform is loaded, against the manifest at 1:1 with no excerpt.
import Prog exposing (Program)


main : Program
main = Prog.say "hello"
